# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific paths.
#
# tools/local.settings.ps1 is the ONLY file permitted to contain absolute paths
# from a particular workstation. Everything committed refers to those by name
# and resolves them at run time; tools/local.settings.ps1.example shows the
# shape. Git does not forget, so a path committed once is in every future clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tools/local.settings.ps1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party Papyrus vendored for COMPILATION ONLY.
#
# These are other people's mods, kept locally so our scripts can compile against
# their types. None is our work and none is ours to redistribute:
#
#   SkyrimNetApi.psc   SkyrimNet          (MinLL)
#   MARAS.psc          MARAS              (native SKSE interface)
#
# docs/BUILD_PLUGIN.md tells a builder where to get each. A slightly worse
# first-build experience and a much better licensing position.
#
# Romantasy.psc is NOT here: it is our own eleven-line declaration of the five
# native functions we call, written from Romantasy's public documentation rather
# than copied from it. Without it nothing compiles.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/scripts/SkyrimNetApi.psc
/src/scripts/MARAS.psc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled Papyrus. Rebuilt from src/scripts by tools/build.ps1, and shipped in
# release archives rather than tracked - same policy as SkyrimNet-Kinship.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Scripts/*.pex

# The Creation Kit plugin is a binary built by hand per docs/BUILD_PLUGIN.md.
# Tracked deliberately: it is 333 bytes, ESL-flagged, and rebuilding it means
# ten minutes of clicking in the CK rather than running a script.
!SNRom_Integration.esl

# Build scratch: vanilla sources unpacked from the game's own Scripts.zip, and
# superseded artifacts. Bethesda's and ours respectively, neither to be tracked.
/.build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation held back until the next Romantasy release closes the gaps it
# describes. Accurate and candid about known defects and unfinished work - but
# not the first thing a new reader should meet, and some of it describes
# behavior that release is expected to change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/BACKLOG.md
/docs/ANNOUNCEMENT.md
/docs/KINSHIP_INTEGRATION_REQUEST.md
/docs/KINSHIP_INTEGRATION_RESPONSE.md
/docs/SPEC_parentage_mod.md

# Local scratch, editors, OS
*.bak
*.vortex_backup
*.log
.vs/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Release archives. Rebuildable by tools/package.ps1; GitHub Releases is the
# right home for the ones that matter.
/dist/
